 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Cut the 3,681-model Laptop list to 20 archetype lines (historic icons, then lines by start year) whose versions are generations from the retrieved Wikipedia pages or names from the old data, plus 20 market-covering current models in m (Acer, Lenovo, Dell, Alienware, HP, ASUS, Samsung, LG, MSI, System76, Tuxedo). Dropped the long tail of vintage and regional SKUs (AST, Bondwell, NEC, Medion, Epson, Olivetti, GRiD, etc.) as SKU noise; GRiD Compass belongs with vintage portables if wanted. Detachables moved from the Laptop list (ROG Flow Z13, ThinkPad X12, Spectre x2, Miix) into Detachable 2-in-1. Dell XPS versions carry no years: the XPS page did not give per-model years. Surface Laptop first-generation year left blank (page unclear). Gaming, business, rugged, convertible kept as types."
}